This is a **folded-cascode OTA** with an NMOS input pair. A single high-impedance node at the output keeps the phase margin high, and the 1 pF load acts as the compensation capacitor. All bias voltages come from the 10 µA reference using two resistors. These numbers are hand estimates and have not been simulated yet.

**Why this topology**
- **Gain:** A plain 5T OTA reaches only about 30–45 dB in sky130, which is marginal against the 45 dB target. Cascoding the output gives more than 60 dB.
- **Bandwidth:** UGB ≈ gm1 / (2π·(CL + Cpar)). With gm1 ≈ 2.1 mS (150 µA per side at gm/Id ≈ 14), UGB ≈ 290 MHz. That leaves margin over the 150 MHz target.
- **Non-dominant poles:** The folded nodes are at about gm_cas / C_fold ≈ 1.2 mS / 150 fF ≈ 1.3 GHz. The mirror node is also at about 1.3 GHz. This should give a phase margin above 65°.
- **Power:** Tail current is 300 µA, the PMOS sources carry 2×250 µA, and the bias branches take 2×10 µA. That is about 0.52 mA, or about 0.94 mW, under the 2 mW limit.
- **Polarity:** If vinp rises, MN1 draws more current, so the cascode on the mirror side carries less. The mirror then sinks less at vout. At the same time the vinn side pushes more current into vout. Both effects raise vout, so vinp is the non-inverting input.

**Bias generation**
- **ibias pin:** The reference current flows through RN into the diode MB0. This makes the pin voltage the NMOS cascode bias, vnc = Vgs + 10 µA·RN ≈ 0.85 V.
- **Tail:** The node nb, the gate of the MB0 diode, sets the tail current. It equals 10 µA·WT/WN.
- **PMOS bias branch:** MB1 copies the 10 µA reference. That current flows through the PMOS diode MPB and RP, which gives vbp. The PMOS cascode gate is vpc = vbp − 10 µA·RP, set so the top PMOS sit at about 0.25 V Vsd.
- **NMOS mirror:** The bottom mirror is a wide-swing cascode mirror, which converts the differential signal to a single-ended output.

```spice
.subckt dut vinp vinn vout vdd vss ibias
* ---- bias generation ----
* ibias pin voltage = vnc (NMOS cascode gate) = Vgs(MB0) + Iref*RN
RN    ibias nb {RN}
MB0   nb    nb  vss vss nfet W={WN} L={LN}
* PMOS bias branch: 10uA copy -> diode MPB (vbp) -> RP -> vpc
MB1   vpc   nb  vss vss nfet W={WN} L={LN}
RP    vbp   vpc {RP}
MPB   vbp   vbp vdd vdd pfet W={WPB} L={LP}
* ---- input pair + tail ----
MT    tail  nb   vss  vss nfet W={WT} L={LN}
MN1   fa    vinp tail vss nfet W={W1} L={L1}
MN2   fb    vinn tail vss nfet W={W1} L={L1}
* ---- PMOS current sources (fold) ----
MP1   fa    vbp vdd vdd pfet W={WP} L={LP}
MP2   fb    vbp vdd vdd pfet W={WP} L={LP}
* ---- PMOS cascodes ----
MPC1  ca    vpc fa  vdd pfet W={WPC} L={LPC}
MPC2  vout  vpc fb  vdd pfet W={WPC} L={LPC}
* ---- NMOS wide-swing cascode mirror (diff -> single-ended) ----
MNC3  ca    ibias xa  vss nfet W={WNC} L={LNC}
MNC4  vout  ibias xb  vss nfet W={WNC} L={LNC}
MN3   xa    ca    vss vss nfet W={WS} L={LS}
MN4   xb    ca    vss vss nfet W={WS} L={LS}
.ends dut
```

```json
{"params": {
  "W1":  [20, 6, 60],
  "L1":  [0.2, 0.15, 0.5],
  "WT":  [60, 20, 160],
  "WN":  [2, 1, 6],
  "LN":  [1, 0.5, 2],
  "WP":  [70, 20, 200],
  "WPB": [3, 1, 8],
  "LP":  [0.5, 0.3, 1.5],
  "WPC": [30, 8, 100],
  "LPC": [0.25, 0.15, 0.8],
  "WS":  [15, 4, 60],
  "LS":  [0.5, 0.3, 1.5],
  "WNC": [20, 5, 60],
  "LNC": [0.2, 0.15, 0.6],
  "RP":  [25000, 5000, 60000],
  "RN":  [15000, 2000, 50000]
}}
```

**Notes for the optimiser**
- **Currents:** Tail current is 10 µA·WT/WN, and each PMOS source carries 10 µA·WP/WPB. Keep the PMOS current above half the tail current so the cascodes stay on. The initial values give 250 µA against 150 µA.
- **Power:** Some corners of the parameter ranges exceed 2 mW, for example a large WT with a small WN. The power constraint will prune those.
- **Bias resistors:** RP sets the headroom of the top PMOS, and RN sets the headroom of the bottom mirror. Both mainly affect output swing and gain, and change bandwidth very little.
